 Project Objectives ;
The main objective of the Blood Bank Management System is to develop a web-based application that automates and simplifies the management of blood bank operations, including donor records, blood inventory, donations, and blood requests.

Specific Objectives :
1.To maintain donor information efficiently :
Store and manage donor details such as name, blood group, contact information, and donation history.
2.To manage blood inventory effectively :
Track available blood units of different blood groups and maintain accurate stock records.
3.To record and monitor blood donations :
Maintain donation records and update blood stock automatically after successful donations.
4.To process blood requests quickly ;
Enable staff to create, update, and track blood requests from hospitals or patients.
5.To provide blood availability search
Allow users to check the availability of blood units based on blood groups.
6.To reduce manual paperwork
Replace traditional record-keeping methods with a centralized digital system.
7.To improve data accuracy and reliability
Minimize human errors, duplicate records, and data loss through computerized management.
8.To support efficient decision-making
Provide dashboards and reports that help staff monitor blood stock and donation activities.
9.To implement CRUD operations :
Enable Create, Read, Update, and Delete operations for donors, blood inventory, donations, and blood requests.
10.To develop a user-friendly web application ;
Build an intuitive and responsive interface using React and Bootstrap for easy system usage.

Overall Objective :
To design and develop a secure, efficient, and user-friendly Blood Bank Management System that automates blood bank operations, improves blood inventory management, and ensures timely access to blood-related information through a web-based platform.
